{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "legend2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 40,
      "width": 1200,
      "height": 90,
      "text": "**Legend** \u2014 \ud83d\udfe3 Agent judgment \u00b7 \ud83d\udd34 Deterministic enforcement \u00b7 \ud83d\udfe0 State reconciliation/journaling. Numbered 1-12, left to right, wrapping to a second row.",
      "color": "#868e96"
    },
    {
      "id": "s1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 200,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 220,
      "text": "**1. Reconcile prior pending activity**\n\nCheck any order still `pending` against REAL broker state (`get_order_status`). The broker is truth, never the journal \u2014 a prior cycle may have died mid-flight. No new order until this is clean.",
      "color": "#f08c00"
    },
    {
      "id": "s2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 460,
      "y": 200,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 220,
      "text": "**2. Read RULES.md**\n\nRe-read the locked rules file at the start of EVERY cycle \u2014 position sizing, caps, circuit breaker, stop distances, prohibitions. Never worked from memory of what it said.",
      "color": "#e03131"
    },
    {
      "id": "s3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 880,
      "y": 200,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 220,
      "text": "**3. Establish account & position state**\n\n`get_account` + `get_positions` \u2014 the broker's real numbers, not the journal's, which can drift. A null drawdown figure is treated as a tripped breaker, not \"fine.\"",
      "color": "#f08c00"
    },
    {
      "id": "s4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1300,
      "y": 200,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 220,
      "text": "**4. Manage exits first**\n\nBefore looking for anything new, per open position: stop/target hit? time stop expired (\u00a76c)? thesis invalidated (\u00a76d)? Exits are exempt from market-hours/circuit-breaker limits.",
      "color": "#9c6ade"
    },
    {
      "id": "s5",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1720,
      "y": 200,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 220,
      "text": "**5. Screen & evaluate candidates**\n\nActively evaluate EVERY watchlist name not already held. Ordinary confidence (3) is a sufficient reason to act \u2014 this is a throughput-built sandbox, not a wait-for-perfect one.",
      "color": "#9c6ade"
    },
    {
      "id": "s6",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2140,
      "y": 200,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 220,
      "text": "**6. Review technical evidence**\n\nmaverick-mcp technicals (RSI/MACD/support-resistance/trend). Is there a setup worth acting on? The agent's own judgment \u2014 deliberately no formula gate.",
      "color": "#9c6ade"
    },
    {
      "id": "s7",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 480,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 220,
      "text": "**7. Apply the news veto**\n\nAdverse news VETOES the entry. Positive news is NEVER a reason to buy \u2014 it can only fail to block one. Missing/unavailable news = skip the entry (\u00a75a), never \"assume clean.\"",
      "color": "#e03131"
    },
    {
      "id": "s8",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 460,
      "y": 480,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 220,
      "text": "**8. Propose stop, target & quantity**\n\nStop at a real technical level inside \u00a76a's 3-12% band. Target must clear the currently-binding \u00a76b reward:risk floor. Size = the SMALLER of \u00a72a risk-based and \u00a72b cap sizing.",
      "color": "#9c6ade"
    },
    {
      "id": "s9",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 880,
      "y": 480,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 220,
      "text": "**9. Deterministic risk validation**\n\nrisk_checker.py re-checks every RULES.md numeric limit in code, independent of the agent's own reasoning \u2014 pure functions, fail-closed on any unknown/non-finite value.",
      "color": "#e03131"
    },
    {
      "id": "s10",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1300,
      "y": 480,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 220,
      "text": "**10. Queue & execute the order**\n\nDecision-time validation is advisory (today's state as a proxy). Execution resolves no earlier than the next real trading day's open \u2014 execution-time price is the sole authority.",
      "color": "#e03131"
    },
    {
      "id": "s11",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1720,
      "y": 480,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 220,
      "text": "**11. Journal evidence & results**\n\n`record_decision` + `record_execution_result` \u2014 every decision, outcome and rejection reason logged, with the specific rule and number, not a mood.",
      "color": "#f08c00"
    },
    {
      "id": "s12",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2140,
      "y": 480,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 220,
      "text": "**12. Reflect at the required cadence**\n\nReview recent decisions/outcomes; check `sample_size` before concluding anything. Never loosen a constraint from a reflection \u2014 only an explicit human decision changes RULES.md.",
      "color": "#9c6ade"
    },
    {
      "id": "warn_news",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 760,
      "width": 2740,
      "height": 70,
      "text": "\u26a0 **Chronology and news-veto discipline are not optional simplifications above:** exits (step 4) always run before new entries are even screened (step 5), and step 7's veto can only BLOCK a candidate that already cleared steps 5-6 on technicals \u2014 news alone never creates a BUY.",
      "color": "#868e96"
    },
    {
      "id": "grp_backtest",
      "type": "group",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 860,
      "width": 2860,
      "height": 300,
      "label": "Backtest-specific branch \u2014 steps 5-10 above collapse into ONE harness-orchestrated cycle"
    },
    {
      "id": "b1",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 40,
      "y": 920,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 200,
      "text": "**Point-in-time data collection**\n\nHarness fetches technicals/news/bars as of the simulated date only \u2014 nothing that would not have existed yet.",
      "color": "#e03131"
    },
    {
      "id": "b2",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 440,
      "y": 920,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 200,
      "text": "**Identity masking**\n\nReal ticker/company identities reshuffled per run (`anonymize.py`). The agent never sees or can recover the real mapping.",
      "color": "#e03131"
    },
    {
      "id": "b3",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 840,
      "y": 920,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 200,
      "text": "**Prompt construction**\n\nOne rendered prompt per simulated trading day \u2014 masked inputs, the currently-binding rules threshold, no trade-count quota anywhere in it.",
      "color": "#e03131"
    },
    {
      "id": "b4",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1240,
      "y": 920,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 200,
      "text": "**Trading-agent decision**\n\nThe agent calls NO tools in backtest \u2014 replies with the JSON decision object only, reasoning over exactly what the prompt shows it.",
      "color": "#9c6ade"
    },
    {
      "id": "b5",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1640,
      "y": 920,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 200,
      "text": "**Next-day execution**\n\nA decision made on day T is queued and resolves no earlier than day T+1's real open \u2014 no same-day lookahead, ever.",
      "color": "#e03131"
    },
    {
      "id": "b6",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2040,
      "y": 920,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 200,
      "text": "**Intraday stop/target simulation**\n\nReal 15-min bars: opening gap -> time-stops -> queued SELLs at 09:30 -> first-bar stop/target -> queued BUYs at 09:45 (re-validated on 09:45-known marks only) -> bar walk.",
      "color": "#e03131"
    },
    {
      "id": "b7",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2440,
      "y": 920,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 200,
      "text": "**Durable state & evidence commit**\n\nEssential cycle data (decision, portfolio state, risk checks, evidence) commits atomically before best-effort observability \u2014 a crash after commit never double-trades.",
      "color": "#e03131"
    }
  ],
